WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:01.150
I am thrilled this evening.

2
00:00:01.150 --> 00:00:03.000
We have an excellent show for you tonight.

3
00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:05.790
And as always, whoever has the most whammy points

4
00:00:05.790 --> 00:00:07.800
will go straight onto a double bonus,

5
00:00:07.800 --> 00:00:08.867
but before we get to that.

6
00:00:08.867 --> 00:00:11.130
(audience laughing)

7
00:00:11.130 --> 00:00:12.750
I'm sorry, who the hell was that?

8
00:00:12.750 --> 00:00:13.880
Now, wait a minute, wait a minute.

9
00:00:13.880 --> 00:00:14.780
Which camera is mine?

10
00:00:14.780 --> 00:00:16.680
Am I camera three, or am I camera two?

11
00:00:16.680 --> 00:00:17.513
Or is it one?

12
00:00:17.513 --> 00:00:20.170
Stan, goddammit, can somebody tell me what camera I am?!

13
00:00:20.170 --> 00:00:21.003
[Conan] Okay.

14
00:00:21.003 --> 00:00:22.673
Sir, please, excuse me, sir!

15
00:00:22.673 --> 00:00:24.960
Sir!
Three, two, one,

16
00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:26.010
and here we go!

17
00:00:26.010 --> 00:00:27.670
Hello, folks, and welcome back

18
00:00:27.670 --> 00:00:31.190
to America's favorite game show, Fill in the Blanks!

19
00:00:31.190 --> 00:00:32.460
I am your host--
(audience cheering)

20
00:00:32.460 --> 00:00:33.360
That's right!

21
00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:34.803
(audience cheering)

22
00:00:34.803 --> 00:00:35.636
No.

23
00:00:36.987 --> 00:00:38.465
No.

24
00:00:38.465 --> 00:00:41.500
It truly is America's favorite!

25
00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:44.880
I am your host Reed Newport, just like the cigarettes!

26
00:00:44.880 --> 00:00:45.728
Yep!

27
00:00:45.728 --> 00:00:47.660
(audience laughing)

28
00:00:47.660 --> 00:00:49.970
Menthols are the ones I prefer most,

29
00:00:49.970 --> 00:00:52.220
and the survey says!
(bell dinging)

30
00:00:52.220 --> 00:00:53.373
All right, look, hey!

31
00:00:54.780 --> 00:00:55.613
I am sorry, sir.

32
00:00:55.613 --> 00:00:57.480
I think you're in the wrong studio.

33
00:00:57.480 --> 00:00:59.820
500 more points, and that will take us straight

34
00:00:59.820 --> 00:01:01.620
to an All or Nothing.

35
00:01:01.620 --> 00:01:03.520
Conan, I don't think that guy can hear you.

36
00:01:03.520 --> 00:01:04.700
I've heard about him.

37
00:01:04.700 --> 00:01:07.700
He's this leftover game show host from the '80s.

38
00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:10.050
He's wandered the studio lot for decades

39
00:01:10.050 --> 00:01:11.870
since his show was canceled.

40
00:01:11.870 --> 00:01:16.320
Let's say hello to Natasha from Clearwater, Florida!

41
00:01:16.320 --> 00:01:19.320
(audience cheering)

42
00:01:25.073 --> 00:01:28.210
Natasha, I understand that you're an algebra teacher.

43
00:01:28.210 --> 00:01:30.150
How long have you been an algebra teacher?

44
00:01:30.150 --> 00:01:30.983
12 years.

45
00:01:30.983 --> 00:01:31.816
12 years!

46
00:01:31.816 --> 00:01:33.849
Well, that's just about how long it takes.

47
00:01:33.849 --> 00:01:36.490
(audience laughing)

48
00:01:36.490 --> 00:01:38.590
Excuse me, would you please leave my audience alone?

49
00:01:38.590 --> 00:01:41.100
Hey, let's get to know Dickie St. Wayne,

50
00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:42.680
all the way from Amarillo, Texas.

51
00:01:42.680 --> 00:01:44.960
Dickie, I understand you run a honey farm.

52
00:01:44.960 --> 00:01:45.833
What's that like?

53
00:01:46.850 --> 00:01:47.716
Sticky.

54
00:01:47.716 --> 00:01:49.990
(audience laughing)

55
00:01:49.990 --> 00:01:52.164
Dickie, you just said our secret word!

56
00:01:52.164 --> 00:01:53.024
(alarm blaring)

57
00:01:53.024 --> 00:01:56.191
(audience applauding)

58
00:01:57.573 --> 00:01:58.656
No, no, no!

59
00:01:59.544 --> 00:02:02.544
Connie, tell 'em what they've won!

60
00:02:03.448 --> 00:02:04.281
Look at that!

61
00:02:04.281 --> 00:02:05.717
It's our grand prize!

62
00:02:05.717 --> 00:02:08.717
(audience cheering)

63
00:02:10.857 --> 00:02:12.003
Looking good, Connie!

64
00:02:13.190 --> 00:02:16.610
It's a personal water sport device from Takahomi.

65
00:02:16.610 --> 00:02:18.870
Now, this is strictly illegal in the United States,

66
00:02:18.870 --> 00:02:21.510
but folks, if you're on international waters,

67
00:02:21.510 --> 00:02:22.730
let it rip!
I'm sorry.

68
00:02:22.730 --> 00:02:24.490
You know, we cannot afford that!

69
00:02:24.490 --> 00:02:25.340
We can't afford that!

70
00:02:25.340 --> 00:02:27.800
And the survey says!
(buzzer sounds)

71
00:02:27.800 --> 00:02:28.830
Oh!

72
00:02:28.830 --> 00:02:29.663
Tough break!

73
00:02:32.100 --> 00:02:34.270
I honestly don't know what's going, I...

74
00:02:34.270 --> 00:02:36.730
30 seconds on the clock, and it's just about time

75
00:02:36.730 --> 00:02:38.940
to find out what's inside the box!

76
00:02:38.940 --> 00:02:41.360
We've eliminated both Carl and Brenda,

77
00:02:41.360 --> 00:02:42.640
which leaves only Carrie,

78
00:02:42.640 --> 00:02:44.990
and I hope she doesn't spend all of her gimme points

79
00:02:44.990 --> 00:02:48.302
before it's time to pull that lever!

80
00:02:48.302 --> 00:02:51.153
(audience cheering)

81
00:02:51.153 --> 00:02:51.986
No!

82
00:02:53.579 --> 00:02:55.789
There's no!
(audience cheering)

83
00:02:55.789 --> 00:02:57.320
No!
Pull that lever!

84
00:02:57.320 --> 00:02:58.990
It's not a game show!

85
00:02:58.990 --> 00:03:00.615
It's lever time!

86
00:03:00.615 --> 00:03:01.665
[Conan] No!

87
00:03:01.665 --> 00:03:02.963
Here comes the lever!

88
00:03:04.117 --> 00:03:05.401
Stop!

89
00:03:05.401 --> 00:03:06.250
Stop it!

90
00:03:06.250 --> 00:03:07.500
There's no game show!

91
00:03:07.500 --> 00:03:08.820
Reed!

92
00:03:08.820 --> 00:03:10.680
Reed Newport, can you hear me?!

93
00:03:10.680 --> 00:03:12.320
Did someone say my name?

94
00:03:12.320 --> 00:03:13.657
Do I hear my name somewhere?

95
00:03:13.657 --> 00:03:16.340
I can see the outline of a very tall girl scout.

96
00:03:16.340 --> 00:03:18.380
Oh, for God's sake!
(audience laughing)

97
00:03:18.380 --> 00:03:19.740
Just stop! Stop!

98
00:03:19.740 --> 00:03:21.150
Well, the only way to stop it, Conan,

99
00:03:21.150 --> 00:03:22.443
is to press that red button right in front of you.

100
00:03:22.443 --> 00:03:24.659
Listen, there's no red button.

101
00:03:24.659 --> 00:03:26.532
Pull that lever!
No!

102
00:03:26.532 --> 00:03:29.011
(audience cheering)

103
00:03:29.011 --> 00:03:29.844
No!

104
00:03:30.900 --> 00:03:32.280
There's no lever!

105
00:03:32.280 --> 00:03:33.370
There's no red button!
Conan.

106
00:03:33.370 --> 00:03:34.926
Looks like it's time to ring that bell!

107
00:03:34.926 --> 00:03:37.300
There's no bell!
(bell ringing)

108
00:03:37.300 --> 00:03:38.905
Ready to take another spin at the wheel?!

109
00:03:38.905 --> 00:03:40.760
There's no wheel!

110
00:03:40.760 --> 00:03:43.770
Reed, this is painful and hard for you to accept.

111
00:03:43.770 --> 00:03:45.950
Your show went away

112
00:03:45.950 --> 00:03:48.299
a long, long time ago.

113
00:03:48.299 --> 00:03:50.090
(audience sighing)
I'm sorry!

114
00:03:50.090 --> 00:03:52.210
I'm sorry, but it did, and this is sad.

115
00:03:52.210 --> 00:03:53.663
It's time to stop.

116
00:03:55.988 --> 00:03:57.580
Well, maybe you're right.

117
00:03:57.580 --> 00:04:00.070
Maybe it is time to take a break.

118
00:04:00.070 --> 00:04:03.660
Maybe I should pack up my things and cash in my pension.

119
00:04:03.660 --> 00:04:04.923
No, no, no, I--
(audience sighing)

120
00:04:04.923 --> 00:04:05.756
It's okay.
No.

121
00:04:05.756 --> 00:04:06.589
It's what he needs to do.

122
00:04:06.720 --> 00:04:10.970
This is good for me because I think I really should move

123
00:04:10.970 --> 00:04:12.772
all the way to the bonus round!

124
00:04:12.772 --> 00:04:17.532
No!
(audience cheering)

125
00:04:17.532 --> 00:04:18.417
That's right, folks!

126
00:04:18.417 --> 00:04:20.840
The bonus round is just like the lightning round,

127
00:04:20.840 --> 00:04:22.380
except it's nowhere near as fast.

128
00:04:22.380 --> 00:04:24.199
Here I go into the isolation booth.

129
00:04:24.199 --> 00:04:25.060
Ladies and gentlemen--
Now, when I'm in here,

130
00:04:25.060 --> 00:04:26.516
circle takes the X, and I won't hear

131
00:04:26.516 --> 00:04:27.626
anything you say.
I'm sorry.

132
00:04:27.626 --> 00:04:28.703
That's Reed Newport.

133
00:04:28.703 --> 00:04:30.350
We'll get him a doctor.

134
00:04:30.350 --> 00:04:31.740
He'll be fine.

135
00:04:31.740 --> 00:04:32.970
Terrific show tonight.

136
00:04:32.970 --> 00:04:35.210
From the new movie Overboard,

137
00:04:35.210 --> 00:04:37.414
Eva Longoria is on the program!

138
00:04:37.414 --> 00:04:39.680
(audience cheering)

139
00:04:39.680 --> 00:04:40.513
Very exciting!

140
00:04:40.513 --> 00:04:42.350
[Reed] Conan, Conan, I think she prefers

141
00:04:42.350 --> 00:04:44.740
to be called Ava Longoria.
No, no, no, it's Eva!

142
00:04:44.740 --> 00:04:45.573
It's not Ava!

143
00:04:45.573 --> 00:04:47.470
Shut up!
Well.

144
00:04:47.470 --> 00:04:49.490
From the HBO series Westworld,

145
00:04:49.490 --> 00:04:51.236
Luke Hemsworth is on the program!

146
00:04:51.236 --> 00:04:53.093
(audience cheering)

147
00:04:53.093 --> 00:04:57.220
[Reed] Luke Hemsworth, all the way from Amarillo, Texas!

148
00:04:57.220 --> 00:04:58.880
He runs a honey farm.

149
00:04:58.880 --> 00:05:01.940
All right.
(audience laughing)

150
00:05:01.940 --> 00:05:04.520
Shut up.
(audience laughing)

151
00:05:04.520 --> 00:05:05.630
Thrilled, musical guests

152
00:05:05.630 --> 00:05:08.025
Ben Harper, Charlie Musselwhite on the show!

153
00:05:08.025 --> 00:05:09.877
(audience cheering)

154
00:05:09.877 --> 00:05:12.230
[Reed] Conan, is that your final answer?

155
00:05:12.230 --> 00:05:14.080
Would you like to phone the audience?

156
00:05:15.330 --> 00:05:16.350
We're gonna take a break.

157
00:05:16.350 --> 00:05:17.183
We're gonna take a break!

158
00:05:17.183 --> 00:05:18.030
We'll be right back.

159
00:05:18.030 --> 00:05:19.338
Jimmy, take it away.

160
00:05:19.338 --> 00:05:20.171
(audience cheering)

161
00:05:20.171 --> 00:05:21.550
Promotional consideration for,

162
00:05:21.550 --> 00:05:23.155
I beg your pardon?

163
00:05:23.155 --> 00:05:23.988
What's the matter?

164
00:05:23.988 --> 00:05:25.310
Everything's going just fine!

165
00:05:25.310 --> 00:05:27.057
Look, pull that lever!

166
00:05:27.057 --> 00:05:28.283
Pull that lever!

167
00:05:28.283 --> 00:05:29.639
Come on in the isolation booth.

168
00:05:29.639 --> 00:05:31.639
[Conan] Oh, it's nice!

